WEBVTT

c1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.000
This is our guide to running an anna daan kitchen at a mid-size temple.

c2
00:00:07.500 --> 00:00:16.000
Anadan serves free cooked meals to any visitor, regardless of caste or background. It is a sacred obligation.

c3
00:00:16.500 --> 00:00:26.000
The kitchen must be operational by seven in the morning so that meals are ready by eleven thirty for the first serving.

c4
00:00:26.500 --> 00:00:35.000
Ingredients for the day come from donations. The stock is checked at five thirty each morning by the head sevayat.

c5
00:00:35.500 --> 00:00:45.000
Rice, dal, sabzi, and roti form the base menu. On festival days a mahaprashad is prepared instead, with additional sweet items.

c6
00:00:45.500 --> 00:00:55.000
Hygiene is critical. All cooking is done barefoot after ritual purification. No leather items are permitted inside the kitchen.

c7
00:00:55.500 --> 00:01:06.000
The daily count of meals served is recorded in the kitchen register. This number is reported to the trust board every week.

c8
00:01:06.500 --> 00:01:16.000
Any prashad left after the final serving is not stored. It is either finished by staff or respectfully composted.
